WEBVTT

00:02:54.050 --> 00:02:57.890
We'll block them off on three sides, then lure them out.

00:02:58.390 --> 00:02:59.720
And after that?

00:03:03.230 --> 00:03:04.960
Whatever the situation demands!

00:03:41.200 --> 00:03:43.460
Those guys just now... debt collectors?

00:03:46.670 --> 00:03:48.170
Yes...

00:03:48.170 --> 00:03:50.070
Money you two borrowed?

00:03:53.780 --> 00:03:55.370
It's not, is it?

00:03:57.280 --> 00:03:58.680
Our mother...

00:04:01.020 --> 00:04:02.490
Your mother?

00:04:03.420 --> 00:04:04.760
Last year...

00:04:04.760 --> 00:04:06.380
And then you two...

00:04:07.490 --> 00:04:09.290
The contract was like that.

00:04:11.500 --> 00:04:14.630
So it's not an amount easily paid back?

00:04:14.630 --> 00:04:17.070
They told me to sell an organ.

00:04:17.840 --> 00:04:19.630
And my sister...

00:04:27.750 --> 00:04:29.540
That's terrible.

00:04:30.150 --> 00:04:31.950
What about your old man?

00:04:36.190 --> 00:04:37.650
I see.

00:04:59.480 --> 00:05:01.410
What will you do now?

00:05:01.410 --> 00:05:03.050
Well...

00:05:03.050 --> 00:05:04.850
Any place to go?

00:05:18.130 --> 00:05:20.620
Won't you come to our place?

00:05:21.330 --> 00:05:24.460
We appreciate your concern, but we...

00:05:25.700 --> 00:05:30.110
You know, at our place, there are lots of people like you two.

00:05:30.680 --> 00:05:33.750
Won't you join us?

00:05:33.750 --> 00:05:35.340
Join?

00:05:35.880 --> 00:05:38.140
To fight the devils of this world.

00:05:45.690 --> 00:05:48.990
What we're saying sounds pretty dubious.

00:05:49.290 --> 00:05:52.200
That kind of thing isn't for us.

00:06:05.840 --> 00:06:07.310
They've come.

00:06:08.550 --> 00:06:10.610
The devil children are here.

00:06:15.190 --> 00:06:17.450
Hey, what's this all about?

00:06:18.520 --> 00:06:22.250
It's dangerous, so you two stay here and don't move.

00:06:24.000 --> 00:06:25.460
Just a...

00:06:30.300 --> 00:06:31.430
Kiyoko...

00:07:03.970 --> 00:07:05.800
No good! It won't open!

00:07:06.000 --> 00:07:07.470
This either.

00:07:37.600 --> 00:07:40.330
Those people, do you think...

00:07:41.610 --> 00:07:43.070
No way...

00:07:43.840 --> 00:07:44.870
But...

00:09:49.130 --> 00:09:50.760
Kiyoko, there!

00:11:40.210 --> 00:11:41.510
Let's get away.

00:14:02.050 --> 00:14:03.520
Dropped something.

00:14:08.560 --> 00:14:10.030
You're...

00:14:15.570 --> 00:14:17.300
You were with that monster.

00:14:17.740 --> 00:14:19.200
Monster?

00:14:22.370 --> 00:14:24.840
Are you sure it wasn't a strange dream?

00:14:29.050 --> 00:14:30.750
Could you let us out now?

00:14:30.750 --> 00:14:32.550
Excuse me, driver!

00:14:37.460 --> 00:14:39.720
That's dangerous, doing that.

00:14:39.720 --> 00:14:42.060
What are you trying to do to us?

00:14:42.160 --> 00:14:45.890
We won't do anything to you. We'd just like your company for a bit.

00:14:47.770 --> 00:14:51.960
The Countess says she'd like to meet you two.

00:14:52.500 --> 00:14:54.030
The Countess?

00:15:31.980 --> 00:15:34.710
The Right Honorable the Countess of Werdenberg.

00:15:37.310 --> 00:15:39.080
It's so good of you to come.

00:15:41.590 --> 00:15:43.950
Is there something you want from us?

00:15:44.520 --> 00:15:47.360
I thought we might dine together.

00:15:47.360 --> 00:15:50.490
If you've something to say, please say it here.

00:15:50.490 --> 00:15:52.930
We're not acquainted. We've got no reason to eat together.

00:15:53.530 --> 00:15:58.900
Oh, there's more between us than you realize, Miss Kiyoko Madoka.

00:16:00.500 --> 00:16:01.940
And Tatsuya.

00:16:03.670 --> 00:16:05.940
How do you know our...

00:16:06.480 --> 00:16:10.310
Let's speak about it over dinner.

00:16:15.820 --> 00:16:17.310
Looks good!

00:16:17.660 --> 00:16:20.930
A dinner has been prepared for each of you.

00:16:20.930 --> 00:16:25.030
If you two don't eat, we'll have to throw it away.

00:16:25.030 --> 00:16:27.220
Is that fair to those who made it?

00:16:27.930 --> 00:16:30.590
You've come all the way here. Why not eat?

00:16:32.900 --> 00:16:36.700
After we eat, you'll let us leave, right?

00:16:37.170 --> 00:16:39.640
You have my word.

00:16:40.980 --> 00:16:43.040
Show these two to the lounge.

00:16:43.680 --> 00:16:47.980
I'm sure you're tired. Please relax for a while.

00:17:01.400 --> 00:17:04.420
It's almost like we're still dreaming.

00:17:05.540 --> 00:17:07.830
Was that thing today really a dream?

00:17:09.040 --> 00:17:10.840
It couldn't be.

00:17:24.190 --> 00:17:25.660
Let's get away.

00:17:43.840 --> 00:17:45.310
And then?

00:17:47.310 --> 00:17:49.780
Really? That's to be expected.

00:19:00.850 --> 00:19:04.860
If you did that well on your first mission, it was a great success.

00:19:04.860 --> 00:19:06.580
I commend you.

00:19:07.190 --> 00:19:10.020
But the hard part is still to come.

00:19:10.430 --> 00:19:13.190
But are those two really...

00:19:13.930 --> 00:19:15.630
It's hard to believe.

00:19:15.630 --> 00:19:18.030
Yes, it's certain.

00:19:22.270 --> 00:19:25.400
What's going to happen to us?

00:19:27.080 --> 00:19:32.410
Those three today, this woman just now, why are they approaching us?

00:19:33.580 --> 00:19:35.380
It's about Dad, huh?

00:19:38.590 --> 00:19:40.290
Mom said so.

00:19:40.290 --> 00:19:44.230
She said there's no doubt people will come for us because of Dad.

00:19:44.230 --> 00:19:45.660
When they do...

00:19:47.360 --> 00:19:48.990
Get away.

00:20:03.350 --> 00:20:05.710
Here you are. Please change into these.

00:20:07.790 --> 00:20:10.490
We can't wear these?

00:20:10.490 --> 00:20:16.650
Dinner is formal. We will clean your garments while you dine.

00:21:04.510 --> 00:21:06.310
Well this is a disgrace.

00:21:08.250 --> 00:21:10.240
What, now you come?

00:21:10.710 --> 00:21:13.880
I didn't think it would be necessary for me to take part.

00:21:13.880 --> 00:21:16.510
Your optimism was a mistake.

00:21:18.190 --> 00:21:19.660
So what's next?

00:21:22.560 --> 00:21:25.720
We take both of them back tonight.

00:21:26.700 --> 00:21:28.160
Tonight?

00:21:29.970 --> 00:21:33.800
Before the devils imbue them with their "wisdom."

00:21:33.800 --> 00:21:36.800
That's what the Professor wants too.

00:23:25.120 --> 00:23:28.120
We'll live without relying on anyone, just as we have until now.

00:23:28.120 --> 00:23:30.390
Because we're the children of the terrorist who caused the incident.

00:23:30.390 --> 00:23:31.820
But what's it got to do with us...

00:23:31.820 --> 00:23:32.660
Is that what...

00:23:32.660 --> 00:23:34.290
...if our parent is a terrorist?

00:23:34.290 --> 00:23:35.330
...you wanted to make us say?

00:23:35.330 --> 00:23:36.730
What if they're killed?

00:23:36.730 --> 00:23:38.530
Gilgamesh said you were...

00:23:38.530 --> 00:23:39.430
I don't know!

00:23:39.430 --> 00:23:40.430
...devils.

00:23:40.430 --> 00:23:41.330
How could I know that?

00:23:41.330 --> 00:23:41.930
At any rate...

00:23:41.930 --> 00:23:42.670
Not by you...

00:23:42.670 --> 00:23:43.470
...we have to get away!

00:23:43.470 --> 00:23:44.640
...and not by that Countess!

00:23:44.640 --> 00:23:44.900
No...

00:23:44.900 --> 00:23:46.600
That's uncalled for! Please don't!

00:23:46.600 --> 00:23:49.500
So that's it? I've heard absurd things before, but this is too much!

00:23:49.710 --> 00:23:50.510
Let's go!

00:23:50.510 --> 00:23:53.030
We don't want to be used by anyone.
